coder v0.0.0-devel

USAGE:
  coder exit-node

  Exit nodes terminate workspace egress, enforce policy, and report flows.

  Aliases: exitnode

  Exit nodes are tailnet peers that workspace agents route outbound TCP, UDP,
  and DNS traffic through. Each flow is checked against a policy and reported to
  coderd. Agents older than API 2.14 cannot consume replica-aware
  configurations. Restart workspaces on the new agent before binding exit nodes.

SUBCOMMANDS:
    create      Create an exit node and print its token
    delete      Delete an exit node
    list        List exit nodes in an organization
    replicas    List replicas of an exit node
    server      Run an exit node

———
Run `coder --help` for a list of global options.
